  "details": "I find Votekick severely inadequate for actually moderating pubic instances. Most fail or can't even start regardless of how obnoxious the user was.\n\nI'll throw out some ideas I have in a list and get talking in the comments\n\n- Votekick polling threshold should be influenced by ratio of players who have the Target blocked already\n\n- Votekick polling threshold should be influenced by Target's Account Standing and Trust Rank\n\n- Votekick prompt should only be given to players who have been near or interacted with Target recently. Players on the other end of the map tend to always say No which ruins polling numbers\n\n- Less abusable conditions to start a votekick. I saw somebody literally just rejoin the instance and become immune then go back to harassing people\n\n- Reconsider adding more conditions where users can see who started the votekick",
